From 242f38b0ac2882d7cc9e28af2bf3502737913c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:33:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: misplay report - driver signals, misplay.py, `misplays`
 command, report section

Why: simulated win rates barely track real ones (rank correlation 0.24) and control decks are
underrated by 17-27 points; to fix Forge's per-card AI hints we first need to know which cards
the AI holds, wastes or points badly. This adds per-player misplay signals to the driver and a
ranked per-card report.

Done:
- ForgeBridge.java Tracker (only the Tracker class, a contiguous import block after the existing
  imports, and two lines in the per-player section of runGameUnchecked): new per-player fields
  endHand, endHandLands, idleOwn, idleOpp, counter, removal, roles (definitions in
  mtgsim/bridge/AGENTS.md). Own read-only mana check, because ComputerUtilMana.canPayManaCost can
  roll MyRandom (isManaSourceReserved) and writes AiCardMemory.
- mtgsim/misplay.py (pure functions; old runs fall back to "seen but never cast"), `misplays
  RUN_DIR [--deck] [--top] [--json] [--forge-dir]` in cli.py, a `misplays` key in match /
  gauntlet / matrix summaries, the "Likely AI misplays" report section, tests/test_misplay.py
  (16 tests), docs in mtgsim/AGENTS.md, mtgsim/bridge/AGENTS.md, tests/AGENTS.md.
- Unit tests: 206 pass, 1 skipped (integration, no Forge), with MTGSIM_HOME=$(mktemp -d).

Verified (unchanged games):
- First driver version (before the refinements below): 60 of 60 games identical to the original
  driver (f8d0f28) in winner_seat, turns, first_seat, seats, seed and every player's opening /
  drawn / played / mulligans / turns / life / lossReason. Matches, seed 1, 20 games each:
  Azorius Control vs Jund Sacrifice, Dimir Uldaros vs Izzet Spellementals, Dimir Midrange vs
  Boros Dwarves. 0 tracker errors in the worker logs.
- Early signal from that run: Azorius Control's Countersculpt was seen in 18 games, never cast,
  and passed 48 counter windows; No More Lies passed 45 (cast 11 times); Jace's Machinations was
  never cast in 15 games seen. Removal target quality was never poor (Forge picks targets with
  the same evaluateCreature).

NOT verified yet (the committed driver):
- After that run the Tracker was refined (legendary second copies are not castable; X costs are
  checked at X = 1; a harmful targeted effect needs an opposing target even when optional;
  effects limited to your own permanents (Get Out's bounce) are not removal; counter windows
  include charms with a Counter mode; skipped-activator card names in the stderr line). It
  compiles, but the unchanged-games run for this version was stopped before it started.

Next steps:
1. Re-run the three matches above with this driver through the engine lock (20 games each,
   --seed 1) and compare every game with the baseline. Baseline runs were in
   $SCRATCH/misplay/base-{ac-js,du-iz,dm-bd}; if the scratchpad is gone, rebuild the baseline from
   a `git archive f8d0f28` copy (the original driver) with the same three commands. Compare per
   game id: status, winner_seat, turns, first_seat, seats, seed, and per player opening, drawn,
   played, mulligans, turns, life, lossReason.
2. Write the README section (the `misplays` command and how to read it) and the VALIDATION.md
   entry ("Misplay tracking": the unchanged-games result plus the first-run numbers above).
3. Screenshot a report with the misplay section at 1100 px and 390 px with Playwright (no page
   scroll), and run `python3 -m mtgsim report` on an old run to check the fallback.
4. Optionally assert the new fields exist in tests/test_integration.py; then run the full suite
   under the lock: flock <lock> python3 -m unittest discover -s tests.
5. Final commit; report fields, comparison result, test counts, sample output, limitations.

